WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.880
Although much of the canon information about&nbsp;
the Mandalorian-Jedi War is still up in the air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.840
here's what we know so far. This is the&nbsp;
history of the Mandalorian-Jedi War explained.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.440
As odd as it sounds, the war started because&nbsp;
the Mandalorians did not understand the Jedi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.200
when they first encountered them. Even&nbsp;
at the end of The Mandalorian season 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.120
the Armorer describes the Jedi&nbsp;
as "an order of sorcerers."

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.360
Due to this lack of understanding, the&nbsp;
Mandalorians created weapons and armor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.320
to better combat these mysterious&nbsp;
new opponents. In 2017, Comicbook.com&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.680
interviewed Dave Filoni about&nbsp;
how the Star Wars: Rebels episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.800
"Trials of the Darksaber" referenced&nbsp;
the Mandalorian-Jedi War. He explained,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.800
"The Mandalorian-Jedi War that&nbsp;
I have in my mind is very much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.760
derived from the oldest style of thinking of&nbsp;
Mandalorians, which was that their weapons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:54.880
their arsenal, their technology had a massive&nbsp;
increase once they collided with the Jedi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.120
and found these force-wielding people that&nbsp;
had abilities they didn't understand."

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.560
More and more animosity occurred between&nbsp;
the Mandalorians and Jedi once the latter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:10.000
group started interfering with the former's&nbsp;
crusades. The 2016 reference book Star Wars:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.640
Aliens of the Galaxy details how a&nbsp;
group of sword-wielding Mandalorians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.040
known as the Mandalorian crusaders&nbsp;
carried out a series of conquests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:24.160
across the galaxy. While in the Inner Rim, the&nbsp;
crusaders devastated a planet called Ubduria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:28.800
out of contempt for the native Ubdurians,&nbsp;
who they viewed as dishonorable cowards.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.880
The Mandalorian crusaders also fought the&nbsp;
Jedi at some point during these missions.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.680
Murals of the Mandalorian crusaders fighting&nbsp;
the Jedi were created and can be seen in a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.320
episodes of Star Wars: The Clone Wars, as&nbsp;
well as one episode of Star Wars: Rebels.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:48.080
Even though Mandalorians and Jedi were at one&nbsp;
point sworn enemies, a member of the former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:54.000
group did create a lightsaber of his own. That&nbsp;
member was Tarre Vizsla, the first Mandalorian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.440
ever inducted into the Jedi Order. Tarre created&nbsp;
a unique black-colored lightsaber called the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:05.760
Darksaber during his time as a Jedi. After he&nbsp;
died, the Jedi kept the saber in the Jedi Temple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:10.960
but during the fall of the Old Republic, members&nbsp;
of House Vizsla raided that temple and reclaimed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:17.520
the saber. They used it to unite their people and&nbsp;
defeat anyone who opposed them, including Jedi.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:23.120
The Darksaber would become a symbol of power to&nbsp;
the Mandalorians and was used to unite them before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.280
and after the Mandalorian-Jedi War.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.560
The Mandalorian-Jedi War became so&nbsp;
heated that, near the end of their wars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:35.520
the Mandalorians turned Concordia, the moon&nbsp;
of their homeworld, into a mining base.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.880
Although the Mandalorians put up&nbsp;
a good fight against the Jedi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:43.920
it was not enough to save their homeworld. The&nbsp;
Mandalorian-Jedi War ended with a final battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:49.840
which caused a cataclysm that scorched much of&nbsp;
Mandalore into a white, uninhabitable wasteland.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.760
The Jedi won the war, but not all&nbsp;
was lost for the Mandalorians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.680
as they created hermetically sealed&nbsp;
domed cities on Mandalore's surface.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.920
Years after the Mandalorian-Jedi War ended,&nbsp;
many Mandalorians, including Satine Kryze,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.840
did not want to continue the cycle of&nbsp;
violence that almost destroyed their planet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.680
They formed a peaceful movement&nbsp;
called the New Mandalorians.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:17.040
Forty-two years before the Battle of Yavin, a&nbsp;
civil war broke out between the New Mandalorians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.040
and the martial traditionalists who&nbsp;
both sought control for Mandalore.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:26.240
The death toll during this war was a primary&nbsp;
reason why Satine became a pacifist for the rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:34.160
of her life. As duchess, Satine rebuilt Mandalore,&nbsp;
and it thrived under her leadership for 20 years.&nbsp;

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.840
Mandalore went on to become an active&nbsp;
participant in the senate of the Galactic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.920
Republic while still remaining neutral&nbsp;
throughout the majority of the Clone Wars.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:48.240
Of course, many Mandalorians still opposed&nbsp;
the New Mandalorians' pacifist ideals and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.440
wanted to return Mandalore to its warrior ways.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:55.440
These same Mandalorians would go on&nbsp;
to form the terrorist organization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.440 --> 00:04:01.200
Death Watch under the leadership of Governor&nbsp;
Pre Vizsla and Satine's sister, Bo-Katan Kryze.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:06.320
Death Watch was initially aligned with Count&nbsp;
Dooku and the Separatists, but they parted ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:12.480
and eventually joined forces with a renegade Sith&nbsp;
lord named Maul to take over Mandalore together.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.480
Maul and Vizsla devised a plan&nbsp;
to make the New Mandalorians look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.720
weak in order to gain the people's trust.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.080
"Death Watch is here to save&nbsp;
you from these intergalactic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.160
gangsters that threaten our great city."

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.920
The plan was successfully carried out, and&nbsp;
Vizsla declared himself ruler of Mandalore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:34.000
but he betrayed Maul and imprisoned him.&nbsp;
It didn't take long for Maul to escape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.760
which allowed Maul to challenge&nbsp;
Vizsla to a duel, which he won.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:42.480
After beheading Vizsla with the Darksaber,&nbsp;
Maul declared himself the new leader of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:47.200
Death Watch and installed a puppet prime&nbsp;
minister while he ruled from the shadows.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:52.320
After becoming ruler of Mandalore,&nbsp;
Maul retained the loyalty of most of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:56.240
the members of Death Watch. But&nbsp;
some members, such as Bo-Katan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:02.240
could not accept the idea of an outsider ruling&nbsp;
Mandalore and led a resistance against him.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:07.120
In the seventh season of The Clone Wars, Maul's&nbsp;
reign is cut short after former Jedi knight Ahsoka&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:12.640
Tano and Bo-Katan team up to launch a full-scale&nbsp;
assault in an attempt to liberate Mandalore from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:16.880
the clutches of the Shadow Collective. Before&nbsp;
ordering the other Shadow Collective leaders to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:22.880
go into hiding, Maul is captured but subsequently&nbsp;
escapes custody in the wake of Order 66.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:29.440
The 2018 spinoff film Solo: A Star Wars Story,&nbsp;
set after the events of The Clone Wars season 7,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:34.320
reveals that Maul established another&nbsp;
crime syndicate called the Crimson Dawn.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:40.000
Even though Bo-Katan and her forces defeated Maul&nbsp;
and freed Mandalore from the Shadow Collective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.880
it didn't take long for the Empire to undo all&nbsp;
that progress. After Bo-Katan refuses to comply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:49.600
with the imperial occupation of her homeworld,&nbsp;
Clan Saxon betrayed her and swore allegiance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:55.760
to Emperor Palpatine. Fortunately, Bo-Katan joined&nbsp;
forces with Clan Wren, the Mandalorian Protectors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:59.360
and members of the Rebel Alliance&nbsp;
to fight back against Clan Saxon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:04.880
Following this victory, Bo-Katan was given the&nbsp;
Darksaber and took up the title of Mand'alor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:08.480
a title assumed by the sole&nbsp;
leader of the Mandalorian people.

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:12.320
Unfortunately, the Empire would strike back&nbsp;
against the remaining Mandalorians in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:18.880
form of the Great Purge. This event saw the&nbsp;
deaths of many Mandalorians across the galaxy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:22.080
and the Empire stealing massive amounts of beskar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:26.400
a metal alloy that Mandalorians use&nbsp;
to create their signature armor.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:31.600
In the season 1 finale of The Mandalorian,&nbsp;
the Tribe's Armorer tells Din Djarin that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:36.800
needs to reunite the Child with his people. That&nbsp;
mission sends Mando on a series of adventures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:42.160
including one that puts him in direct contact with&nbsp;
Bo-Katan and her fellow Mandalorian separatists.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:46.400
Although they don't share Djarin's rigid&nbsp;
adherence to the Mandalorian creed Bo-Katan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:51.200
ultimately helps him on his mission, in exchange&nbsp;
for his help in raiding an Imperial ship.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:55.360
Mando is initially led to believe the separatists&nbsp;
are simply trying to steal weapons from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.360 --> 00:07:00.240
shattered Empire, but it eventually becomes clear&nbsp;
that Bo-Katan is really after the Darksaber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:03.840
now wielded by Moff Gideon.&nbsp;
Living up to her end of the deal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:08.160
she tells Djarin where to find a Jedi,&nbsp;
telling him to seek out Ahsoka Tano.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:13.200
Mando heads to the planet Corvus, a&nbsp;
deforested wasteland where Ahsoka Tano&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:17.760
has been waging a war against the brutal&nbsp;
reign of a figure known as the Magistrate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:21.440
Upon Mando's arrival, he's shepherded&nbsp;
to an audience with the Magistrate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:27.440
who offers him a staff made of pure beskar&nbsp;
in exchange for murdering Ahsoka. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:32.720
he joins forces with Ahsoka following a brief&nbsp;
skirmish when they meet in the Corvus wastelands.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:36.880
Mando offers to help Ahsoka defeat the&nbsp;
Magistrate in exchange for her accepting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:42.240
and training the Child. As expected, the&nbsp;
Magistrate is no match for the duo, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:47.600
Ahsoka is unable to live up to her end of the&nbsp;
deal, telling Mando that she can't train the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:52.080
Child. She's able to speak with him via&nbsp;
the Force, and learns that his real name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:56.640
is Grogu— and that he was trained on Coruscant&nbsp;
before being taken during the fall of the Jedi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:01.840
But she also discovers a great deal of fear,&nbsp;
anger, and darkness in him, and having been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:07.120
close to Anakin Skywalker, she's all too&nbsp;
aware of how those feelings can be exploited.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:13.600
Although Ahsoka is unable or unwilling to train&nbsp;
Grogu, she offers Mando one other way to fulfill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:19.040
his obligation — take him to the planet Tython,&nbsp;
where Grogu may be able to tap into the Force at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:23.600
the site of some ancient temple ruins and&nbsp;
establish a connection with another Jedi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:28.240
In the middle of that process, however,&nbsp;
Grogu is kidnapped by Moff Gideon's forces.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:33.120
Mando gathers a crew to overtake Gideon's&nbsp;
light cruiser and save the Child.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:36.080
After reaching Grogu's cell, Mando battles Gideon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:42.000
ultimately Mando disarms Gideon with the Beskar&nbsp;
spear he received from Ahsoka back on Corvus.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:47.680
After taking Grogu and a shackled Gideon to the&nbsp;
bridge, Mando offers the Darksaber to Bo-Katan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:52.320
but she refuses. Gideon clarifies&nbsp;
that the Darksaber cannot be given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:59.280
and must be won in combat. Their stand-off is&nbsp;
interrupted when a Jedi, Luke Skywalker himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:04.160
arrives to rescue them from a squad of Dark&nbsp;
Troopers and take Grogu away to be trained.

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.480
Will Mando and Grogu's connection last?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:10.000
Or will the events of the Mandalorian-Jedi&nbsp;
war repeat themselves once again?

